    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Set on approximately 11.83 Acres of prime Agricultural Land, this impressive Four-Bedroom detached Bungalow enjoys a superb location fronting the main N-17 Sligo to Galway Road, just 2 minutes from the charming village of Kilkelly, 5-minute drive from the renowned Marian village of Knock and only a 10-minute drive from Knock International Airport. Offering an excellent combination of comfortable family living, top quality Farmland with future one-off residential development potential, this is a property that will appeal to a wide variety of purchasers.\r\n\r\nApproached via a long and spacious driveway, the residence is complemented by a large front Garden which provides an attractive outdoor space. Internally, the property itself is bright and welcoming throughout with windows which allow for an abundance of natural light to fill each room and create a warm and welcoming atmosphere.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation extends to an entrance porch and hallway, a very generous open-plan sitting room and dining area featuring an open fireplace, separate living room also with an open fireplace, kitchen, four spacious bedrooms and a family bathroom. Notably, all four bedrooms benefit from their own En-suite bathroom, offering excellent convenience and flexibility for family living or guest accommodation.\r\n\r\nWhile the house would benefit from some modernisation works being carried out, this presents an exciting opportunity for the successful purchaser to modernise and style the house to their own taste and specification, adding further value to an already substantial property.\r\n\r\nTo the rear stands a detached shed which offers excellent potential for conversion into a workshop, studio or recreational space, subject to any necessary consents. The surrounding Lands are of excellent quality grassland throughout and include some additional farm sheds which could easily lend itself to equestrian use or easy conversion to stables.\r\n\r\nA further standout feature of this property is the extensive road frontage along an L.I.S Road side Road, offering potential for a one-off residential building site subject to the appropriate planning permission. This adds significant long-term appeal and investment potential to an already versatile holding.\r\n\r\nRarely does a property come to the market offering an attractive combination of residential accommodation, top quality Agricultural Lands, future development potential and a highly accessible location. Early viewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate all that this unique property has to offer.\r\n\r\nTo arrange a viewing, request a map or any further particulars please contact the sole selling agent John Higgins Auctioneer on 094 9631372."
      },
